    "rationale": "No defensible morpheme paradigm survives the evidence threshold. The apparent shared substrings in the candidate hints (UM, IGHT, EAT, ED, etc.) do not show stable compositional meanings across contrasting residues: e.g. -UM would have to mean something like 'hum/rumble', but RUM, BROKENHUM, WAVERHUM, LAYERHUM, and SPLITHUM do not decompose into a consistent shared morpheme plus a substituting class with predictable whole meanings; likewise -IGHT mixes bright/light, -EAT mixes heat with unrelated residue shapes, -ED mixes RED and WASHED, and other proposed prefixes/suffixes fail the same test. The multi-code strings with '+' and '/' are semantically conjunctive, but the dataset does not provide a securely induced substitutional morphology over their parts under the strict requirement not to promote residual whole symbols into generic ROOT/MISC classes. Since false morphology is worse than a flat analysis, all supplied symbols are treated as lexical.",
